# (`ganesha`) Her runtime'da lezzet; `services.nfs-server.flavor` İçinde in in
# in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in
# in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in in
# `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/meta/services.yml` SPOT, ve `kernel`
# per-inventory override. Ganesha için paketleniyor `Debian` ve `RedHat` Os
# aileleri sadece. Anahtar `nfsd` ayrıcalıklı bir DinD düğümü wedge-prone'dir:
# ihracat henüz kontrol hattı ENOENT'i geri döndürebilir ve `exportfs`
# D-state'de kalabilir. Bir swarm adım atılırsa `Reload NFS exports` Sıkıntılı
# bir çekirdek-NFS Dağı'ndan, you MUST recovery with with `make swarm-clean`
# Ev sahibine; NFS'nin içeri girdiğini [Roundtrip](roundtrip.md).Sen bir
# form-sadece süpürücüye geri düşmezsin, oysa swarm bloke edilir.
msgid "The nfs-server uses the userspace `nfs-ganesha` (`ganesha`) flavor in every runtime; `services.nfs-server.flavor` in `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/meta/services.yml` is the SPOT, and `kernel` is a per-inventory override. Ganesha is packaged for the `Debian` and `RedHat` os families only. Kernel `nfsd` in a privileged DinD node is wedge-prone: the export can be present yet the controller mount returns ENOENT, and `exportfs` can stick in D-state. If a swarm step hangs at `Reload NFS exports` from a stuck kernel-NFS mount, you MUST recover with `make swarm-clean` on the host; see the NFS gotcha in [Roundtrip Loop](roundtrip.md). You MUST NOT fall back to a compose-only sweep while swarm is blocked."
msgstr ""

