# list/head/get; Prometheus adaptörleri geri dönüş/sample sınırları uygular;
# GraphQL ve SQL adaptörleri keyfi giriş dilleri reddeder. **Dört kategorinin
# üçü henüz mevcut değildir:** Sadece sadece sadece sadece sadece sadece
# sadece sadece sadece sadece sadece sadece `openapi_allowlist` (10 rolleri
# rol rol rol rol rol rol rolleri) ve `mcp_passthrough` (4) kullanımdadır ve
# `test_mcp_schema.py` Zaten tam olarak tam olarak gerekli `scope` Bir daha
# önce isimleri `s3_prefix`, `graphql_allowlist` veya `named_query` adaptörün
# gemisi olabilir. The The The The The The The The Prometheus Madde gerçekti
# ve şimdi yarı kapalı: `prometheus_query_range` istemci-chosen `start`, `end`
# ve `step`, Ve konteyner hayır ile koştu `--query.timeout` Her şeyde, bu
# yüzden adaptörü terk ettikten sonra 15s. Prometheus Onun için meşgul 2-
# dakika varsayılan. Şimdi rol geçiyor `--query.timeout` Elde edilenlerden
# elde edilenler `mcp.limits.timeout_seconds`, Ama iki sürüklenemez. **Geri
# dönüş yarısı da kapalıdır ve örnek tavan onu taşıyabilen katmanda
# kapalıdır.** `policy.assert_range` Sözleşmenin kendi başına bir dizi
# sorgunun noktası sayılıyor `result_items`: şemanın ilan ettiği bir araç
# `start`, `end` ve `step` has has has has has has has has has has has has has
# has has has has has has has has have has has has has has has has has has has
# has has has has has has has has has has has has has has has has has has has
# has has has has has has has has has has has has have has has has has has has
# has has has has has has have has has has has has has has has has has has has
# has has has has has has has has has has has has has has has `(end - start) /
# step + 1` Bu tavana karşı kontrol edilir ve reddedilir `range_too_wide` Ve
# sığacak en küçük adım. Yaşama Karşı Prometheus sözleşme, bir gün bir
# dakikalık karar için soruyor 1441 Bir tavana karşı puan 100 Ve adlandırmayı
# reddetti 873-İkinci adım. Nokta kibarlık değildir: adaptör zaten böyle bir
# yanıt verdi 100 satırlar, bu yüzden upstream, sonucun atıldığı bir aralığı
# tarandı ve zaman sadece ne kadar uzun sürdü. Her iki sınır formu da
# Prometheus Kabul edilir, altı saniye ve RFC 3339, Ancak, güvenilmez bir kişi
# dalga geçmek yerine reddedilir, çünkü ölçülemeyen bir aralığın
# sınırlandırılması mümkün değildir. `--query.max-samples` Tipik olarak unset
# kalır: emin olmak için yeterince daha düşük platformun kendi panolarına da
# bağlı olacaktır, bu yüzden tavan herkesin isteklerine ait. Kural geneldir -
# üç dizi argümanı ilan eden bir araçta anahtarlar, bir rol adı üzerinde değil
# - bu yüzden gelecekteki bir dizi upstream devralıyor.
msgid "[x] S3 adapters are restricted to declared bucket prefixes and list/head/get; Prometheus adapters enforce lookback/sample limits; GraphQL and SQL adapters reject arbitrary input languages. **Three of the four categories do not exist yet:** only `openapi_allowlist` (10 roles) and `mcp_passthrough` (4) are in use, and `test_mcp_schema.py` already requires exact `scope` names before an `s3_prefix`, `graphql_allowlist` or `named_query` adapter could ship. The Prometheus clause was real and is now half-closed: `prometheus_query_range` accepts client-chosen `start`, `end` and `step`, and the container ran with no `--query.timeout` at all, so a query the adapter abandoned after 15s kept Prometheus busy for its 2-minute default. The role now passes `--query.timeout` derived from `mcp.limits.timeout_seconds`, so the two cannot drift. **The lookback half is now closed too, and the sample ceiling is closed at the layer that can carry it.** `policy.assert_range` bounds a range query's point count by the contract's own `result_items`: a tool whose schema declares `start`, `end` and `step` has `(end - start) / step + 1` checked against that ceiling and is refused with `range_too_wide` and the smallest step that would fit. Against the live Prometheus contract, a day at one-minute resolution asks for 1441 points against a ceiling of 100 and is refused naming an 873-second step. The point is not politeness: the adapter already truncated such a response to 100 rows, so the upstream was scanning a range whose result was thrown away, and the timeout bounded only how long it did so. Both boundary forms Prometheus accepts are understood, unix seconds and RFC 3339, and an unparseable one is refused rather than waved through, because a range that cannot be measured cannot be bounded. `--query.max-samples` deliberately stays unset: lowering it far enough to matter would also bound the platform's own dashboards, which share the instance, so the ceiling belongs on the adapter's requests rather than on everyone's. The rule is generic — it keys on a tool declaring the three range arguments, not on a role name — so a future range-shaped upstream inherits it."
msgstr ""

