msgstr "```tasks/01_admin.yml`` <./tasks/01_admin.yml>`__ provisions only the administrator in Shopware’s user table. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``services.sso.flavor: oidc``, so no oauth2-proxy fronts the role and the storefront carries no authenticated surface at all; the Keycloak login provider that ```tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` <./tasks/setup/oidc.yml>`__ configures covers the administration backend alone. ``biber`` therefore has no account in any matrix variant and ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` koşulsuz olarak."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` Ve her değişkende çalışır."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>`__) drives the same admin journey and skips on the same flag."
msgstr "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>` ) Aynı yönetim yolculuğu sürüyor ve aynı bayrakta atlar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` and asserts the provider, the base URL and the model, so an unconfigured surface cannot reach a green deploy."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` Ve sağlayıcıyı iddia ediyor, temel URL ve model, bu yüzden yapılandırılmamış bir yüzey yeşil bir dağıtamaz."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, unusable password) plus its own workspace, and binds the endpoint to that pair."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, güvenilmez şifre) artı kendi çalışma alanı ve bu çifte son noktayı bağlar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona ve temel iddialar koşulsuz olarak çalışır."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` Ve her değişkende çalışır."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` in every matrix variant, because the shared persona helper cannot drive this role’s sign-in in any of them. Three independent reasons, each sufficient on its own:"
msgstr "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` Her matrix değişkeninde, çünkü paylaşılan kişi bu rolün işaretini herhangi birinde kullanamaz. Üç bağımsız neden, her biri kendi başına yeterli:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``adapter``:         immutable source contract of a repository-owned adapter. ``category_allowlist`` suits an upstream that switches whole categories and offers no per-tool filter, where a tool allowlist would be unenforceable; ``mcp_passthrough`` fronts an upstream that already speaks MCP instead of translating REST. ``upstream_path`` names that upstream where it lives on the application's own vhost, so the proxy can hide it: reaching it directly walks past the allowlist the adapter exists to enforce. A provider whose upstream is a separate sidecar declares ``upstream_network`` instead and has nothing to hide there."
msgstr "``adapter``: Bir repository ait bir adaptörün kaynak sözleşmesi. ``category_allowlist`` Tüm kategorileri anahtarlayan ve per-tool filtresini sunan bir upstream'e uygun bir araç takılabilirdi; ``mcp_passthrough`` Zaten REST’yi tercüme etmek yerine MCP'yi konuşan bir upstream. ``upstream_path`` Uygulamanın kendi vhost'da nerede yaşadığını gösteren isimler, böylece proxy onu gizleyebilir: adaptörün uygulanmasına izin veren doğrudan yürür. Upstream'in ayrı bir yankar olduğunu söyleyen bir sağlayıcı ``upstream_network`` Bunun yerine ve orada saklanacak bir şey yok."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``aliases``: list of DNS aliases. Default: ``[entity_name]`` for shared_net, ``[]`` for default_net"
msgstr "``aliases``: DNS aliazlar listesi. Varsayılan: ``[entity_name]`` Çünkü shared_net, ``[]`` Çünkü default_net"

# varsayılan varsayılan varsayılan ``True``): Dosya (veya dotted-path entry)
# Mayıs bu tür bir rol için mevcut olabilir. Set Set Set Set ``allowed:
# False`` Bu türün rollerini yasaklamak için, bu yüzden lint tabakası, suçu
# kesin bir nedenle yüzebilir.
msgid "``allowed`` (default ``True``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MAY be present for a role of this type. Set ``allowed: False`` to forbid the file/entry on roles of this type so the lint layer can surface the offence with a precise reason."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible_facts`` only carries ``docker0`` once the daemon has run, and the daemon config is written before that on a fresh node - facts are gathered at play start, and nothing re-gathers them after the install. Reading the fact alone therefore yields nothing on the very run that has to emit the address, which leaves the inner containers pointed at the clearnet resolver and the DinD DNS check failing on a domain only the node dnsmasq knows."
msgstr "``ansible_facts`` Sadece taşırlar ``docker0`` Bir zamanlar daemon koşmuştu ve daemon yapılandırması taze bir node üzerinde daha önce yazılmıştır - gerçekler başlangıçta toplanır ve yüklemeden sonra yeniden toplanmaz. Bu nedenle, adresi yaymak zorunda olan çok koşmakta hiçbir şey vermez, bu da iç konteynerleri açık bir şekilde işaret eder ve DinD DNS kontrol başarısız bir alanda sadece node dnsmasq bilir."

# varsayılan varsayılan varsayılan)
msgid "``ansible`` (default)"
msgstr ""

# varsayılan varsayılan varsayılan) Taşlar `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy
# <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD)MDAD
# çalışır -70 Synapse, Element, her desteklenen köprü, Element Call ve Jitsi
# sunmak için alt-roles. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD, bir MDAD envanterini
# taahhüt ederek verir ``services.matrix.*`` knobs ve MDAD'ın paketlerini
# devre dışı bırakır / Postgres / Redis Bu nedenle merkezi Infinito hizmetleri
# yığını geri döndürür.
msgid "``ansible`` (default) wraps `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD runs ~70 upstream sub-roles to deliver Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Element Call, and Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, and disables MDAD’s bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis so the central Infinito services back the stack."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` is the public S3 endpoint and is reachable without SSO gating."
msgstr "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` Halk S.3 endpoint ve SSO gating olmadan ulaşılabilir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` is read from the play variables unless given as ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` names the block instead of ``ports``, for Discourse's launcher file, whose ``expose:`` list is what becomes ``docker run -p`` there."
msgstr "``application_id`` Verildiği sürece oyun değişkenlerinden okunur. ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` İsimler yerine blok ``ports``, Çünkü Discourse's starter file, kimin ``expose:`` liste ne oluyor ``docker run -p`` Orada."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` of the client doing the discovery."
msgstr "``application_id`` Müşteri keşif yapıyor."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Ev Asistanı, tokeni bu minted hesabına kapsar. Bu dağıtım yöneticisi için gelir, bu yüzden bir çağrı müşteriden gelen yönetici olarak gelir. Entity maruziyeti hala ulaşılabilir. Alet sunucusuna girmek, rolün üzerinde kapılanır ``mcp`` RBAC grubu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Madde en çok token hesabın çağrısına bağlıdır. Bu dağıtım, yönetici hesabı için kişisel erişimin engellenmesine yardımcı olur, bu yüzden bu hesabın haklarını kim sordu. Aracı sunucuya ulaşmak, rolün üzerinde kapılanır ``mcp`` RBAC grubu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: API token, yönetici hesabına karşı verilir, bu yüzden her çağrı, müşteriyi kim sorduysa bu hesabın haklarını taşır. Aracı sunucuya ulaşmak, rolün üzerinde kapılanır ``mcp`` RBAC grubu, yönetmekten ayrı bir hibedir Jenkins."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Kişisel erişim token, karşıtlık ``root`` hesabı ve altında depolanır ``administrator`` Anahtar, bu yüzden her çağrı, istemciyi kimin sorduğu önemli değildir. Aracı sunucuya ulaşmak, rolün üzerinde kapılanır ``mcp`` RBAC grubu, yönetmekten ayrı bir hibedir GitLab."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Web servis token yönetici hesabına karşı verilir, bu yüzden bir çağrı, istemciden kim sorulduğunda bu hesabın haklarını taşır. Ek fonksiyonlar sadece okunur, bu hakların burada ne yapabileceğini sınırlar. Aracı sunucuya ulaşmak, rolün üzerinde kapılanır ``mcp`` RBAC grubu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call comes at at Baserow Müşteriye kim sormaksızın son nokta sahibi olarak ve yalnızca hesabın sahip olduğu bir çalışma alanına ulaşır. Bu, adaptörün izin listesi altında ikinci sınır, bunun yerine bir yedek değil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC grubu, bu ayrı bir hibedir Nextcloud hesap."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject``:    identity MCP calls execute as. ``user`` and ``oidc`` additionally require a ``delegation`` block, because a rendered deployment bearer is a service account no matter what the metadata claims."
msgstr "``auth_subject``: kimlik MCP çağrıları olarak yürütür. ``user`` ve ``oidc`` Ayrıca bir tane gerektirir ``delegation`` Blok, çünkü verilen bir dağıtım ayıcı, metadata iddialarının ne olduğu konusunda bir hizmet hesabıdır."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_type: bearer`` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "``auth_type: bearer`` Keşif verilerden token ile"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth``:            authentication scheme guarding the endpoint."
msgstr "``auth``: Son noktayı koruyan kimlik doğrulama planı."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auto`` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the ``.baudolo-*`` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "``auto`` Danışma ve asla birim başarısız değildir - her reddedilme, dergiye kayıtlıdır ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, Bu yüzden orada bir ev sahibiyseniz, snapshot'ın olmadığını beklersiniz. A specified ``btrfs``/ /``zfs`` Bunun yerine birim başarısız olur, bu da bunu ifade etme noktasıdır. Her snapshot'dan önce, başlatıcı da kaldırır ``.baudolo-*`` Öldürülen bir koşu veri kökü içinde ayrılır."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``backend``: ``cloud`` or ``chezmoi``"
msgstr "``backend``: ``cloud`` veya ``chezmoi``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``base_dir`` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "``base_dir`` (dize): CA dosyaları için temel dizi"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays the dump in the next, so a consumer that boots in between recreates the schema and the replay dies on its own ``CREATE TABLE``. Hence the refusal while a consumer is up."
msgstr "``baudolo-restore --empty`` Bir psql oturumunda şemayı temizliyor ve bir sonraki çöpleri tekrarlıyor, bu yüzden şema ile yeniden oyun yapan bir tüketici ve replay kendi başına ölür ``CREATE TABLE``. Bu nedenle bir tüketici ayağa kalktığında reddedilme."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bench new-site`` uses the central MariaDB’s ``root`` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "``bench new-site`` Merkezin kullanımlarını kullanın MariaDB’s ``root`` İlk dağıtmada per-site DB oluşturmak için."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``biber`` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "``biber`` Sadece içeride hiç var EspoCRM OIDC oto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` Kişi her türlü değişkende çalışır."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bond`` states how tightly a role couples to the service it declares: ``>= 1`` keeps the partner on the same host, ``< 1`` lets it live on its own. The value sits on the consumer's side of the relation, so the pair is directed and the two directions of one pair need not agree."
msgstr "``bond`` Açıklamada çiftlerin servise ne kadar sıkı bir rol oynadığını belirtir: ``>= 1`` partneri aynı hostta tutar, ``< 1`` Kendi başına yaşamasını sağlar. Değer, tüketicinin ilişkisinin tarafında oturur, bu yüzden çift yönlendirilir ve bir çiftin iki yönü aynı fikirde değildir."

